{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2011-09-15","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2021-06-30","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/department/narrative":[{"1":"ESA","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/email":[{"1":"m.chitima@ifad.org"}],"/job-title/narrative":[{"1":"Hub Director","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Chitima, Mawira","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"The overall development objective of the programme is to provide access to a range of financial services for an estimated 6.9 million rural households by 30 June 2019; an increase of over 100 percent from a baseline of about 3.3 million households as at 30 June 2012. This will is achievable through support to a nationwide network of strong, vibrant and sustainable rural financial institutions oriented for engagement with poor.The key policy and institutional objectives include: enhanced human resource capacity and IT support; improved ownership and governance; micro insurance policy framework developed; improved targeting and client literacy; improved social performance standards; improved self-regulatory; grievance redressing mechanisms implemented; effective linkages with commercial banks established;  for raising resources; micro insurance policy and associated regulatory and supervisory framework implemented; and a sustainable, dynamic and vibrant rural financial institutions capable of expanding outreach in depth and breadth in place.","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A12"}],"/description/narrative":[{"1":"More information on how IFAD publish IATI data to ensure the effectiveness of devel